# VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" on each block, top to bottom.
# Watch the server terminal too: handlers log each run, the scheduler logs retries.
@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Delayed one-off job -> 201 SCHEDULED; ~3s later COMPLETED (re-run request 2)
# @name delayed
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SEND_EMAIL", "delayMs": 3000, "payload": { "to": "a@x.com" } }

### 2. Fetch it with its run history
GET {{base}}/jobs/{{delayed.response.body.data.id}}

### 3. Recurring every 5s -> runs list grows on each fetch (request 4)
# @name recurring
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SEND_EMAIL", "intervalMs": 5000, "payload": { "to": "digest@x.com" } }

### 4. Watch the recurring job's runs
GET {{base}}/jobs/{{recurring.response.body.data.id}}

### 5. Cancel the recurring job -> 200 CANCELLED, no more runs (only works while SCHEDULED, not mid-run)
POST {{base}}/jobs/{{recurring.response.body.data.id}}/cancel

### 6. Cancel again -> 409
POST {{base}}/jobs/{{recurring.response.body.data.id}}/cancel

### 7. Always fails: attempts 1,2,3 with 1s, 2s backoff -> FAILED after ~3s (fetch with 8)
# @name failing
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "FAIL_ALWAYS", "maxAttempts": 3 }

### 8. See 3 FAILED runs and lastError
GET {{base}}/jobs/{{failing.response.body.data.id}}

### 9. Random failures: usually succeeds after a retry or two
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "FAIL_RANDOMLY", "payload": { "failRate": 0.7 }, "maxAttempts": 5 }

### 10. Pool saturation: 3 slow reports + 1 high-priority email, pool size 2.
# Send 10a, 10b, 10c, 10d quickly, then 11: 2 RUNNING, the rest wait. The email (priority 9)
# starts before the third report as soon as a worker frees up.
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "GENERATE_REPORT", "payload": { "durationMs": 4000 } }

### 10b
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "GENERATE_REPORT", "payload": { "durationMs": 4000 } }

### 10c
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "GENERATE_REPORT", "payload": { "durationMs": 4000 } }

### 10d
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SEND_EMAIL", "priority": 9, "payload": { "to": "vip@x.com" } }

### 11. Stats: jobs by status, busy workers, heap entries
GET {{base}}/scheduler/stats

### 12. Filter by status
GET {{base}}/jobs?status=SCHEDULED

### 13. Validation: runAt AND delayMs -> 400
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SEND_EMAIL", "runAt": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z", "delayMs": 1000 }

### 14. Unknown type -> 400 with knownTypes
POST {{base}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "NOPE" }
